From 9ea92dc60d3889fb5232295bb9520904ce1f5dd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Dumay <jameswdumay@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 19:22:27 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 29/31] skippy: retain compatible executable graphs with
 scheduler-owned arenas

Keep one additional bounded compute owner with its output/no-output arenas. Preserve full reuse guards and graph-owned sampler eligibility, recover allocation pressure with a fresh scheduler and graph, and account direct host metadata. Test split numerical parity against fresh graphs, alternating lanes and shapes, output classes, KV continuation and injected allocation failure.

Assisted-by: Codex (scammed)
Assisted-by: astrid
